    <title>Retrieval-Gated Decoding Reduces Hallucination in
  Abstractive Summarization</title>
    <updated>2025-02-01T09:00:00Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.01234v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2501.01234v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>  Abstractive summarizers often state facts that are not in the source
document. We introduce retrieval-gated decoding (RGD), which blocks a token when no
retrieved passage of the source supports it.
</summary>
